// Chat.abcl — an actor you converse with.  Each message you send is appended
// to the running story; the actor calls the on-device LLM (llm()) to continue
// it and returns the continuation.  State (the story) persists across messages,
// so the model has memory of the conversation.
//
// Load it resident (/actor/load), then message it (/chat); stories260K is a
// tiny TinyStories model, so "conversation" = collaborative story-continuation.

// chat(msg) keeps a KV-cache session in the model, so each turn only
// processes the new message + its continuation (cost is ~constant per turn,
// instead of growing as the story does).  The conversation memory lives in
// the model's cache; /actor/load starts a fresh session.
class Chat {
  var turns = 0;
  method say(msg) {
    turns = turns + 1;
    return chat(msg);
  }
}

var c = new Chat();
